  "brief": "`nums` is a list of whole numbers and `target` is a whole number. Write `count_pairs_with_sum(nums, target)`, which returns the number of pairs of positions `i < j` with `nums[i] + nums[j] == target`. Equal values at different positions count separately. The answer needs a `long long`.",
  "constraints": [
    "$0 \\le n \\le 180{,}000$ entries, each between -1,000,000 and 1,000,000.",
    "$O(n)$ expected time is the target. Checking every pair is too slow.",
    "Each test has a 5-second limit."
  ],
  "hint": "Keep a hash map of how many times each value has been seen. For each new value `x`, add the count of `target - x`, then record `x`.",
  "starter": "#include <vector>\n#include <unordered_map>\n\nlong long count_pairs_with_sum(std::vector<int> nums, int target) {\n    // your code here\n    return 0;\n}\n",
