  "how": "Submit runs 12 hidden tests. Each answer must equal the expected value.",
  "solution": "#include <vector>\n#include <unordered_map>\n\nlong long count_pairs_with_sum(std::vector<int> nums, int target) {\n    std::unordered_map<int, long long> seen;\n    long long count = 0;\n    for (int x : nums) {\n        auto it = seen.find(target - x);\n        if (it != seen.end()) count += it->second;\n        ++seen[x];\n    }\n    return count;\n}\n",
  "notes": [
    "Each new value pairs with every earlier value equal to `target - x`.",
    "Looking up before recording stops a value pairing with itself.",
    "One pass with a hash map, so the work is $O(n)$."
  ]
}
